source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: Outside a table a `|` separates no token, so Jira shows the first pair and breaks on the second; jiro reads the same. Inside a row the same two runs are in different cells and both break.
-- input.jira --
a\\b|c\\d
-- rendered.html --
<p>a\\b|c<br class="atl-forced-newline" />d</p>
-- want.md --
a\\\\b|c\
d
-- warnings.json --
[]
